        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          HRF Rack 2 is an all-drawer International Standard Payload Rack.  The HRF Rack 2 provides International Space Station (ISS) services and utilities to experiments/instruments installed in the racks.  These include electrical power, command and data handling, cooling air and water, pressurized gases, and vacuum.  The design of the HRF Rack 2 accommodates drawer mounted experiments/ instruments using the International Subrack Interface Standard (ISIS) for structural, power, and data interfaces.
<P>
HRF Rack 2 delivers additional capabilities on-orbit to continue biomedical research on the ISS.  These capabilities include:<P>
<LI>Refrigerated Centrifuge
<LI>Space Linear Acceleration Mass Measurement Device (SLAMMD)
<LI>Rack 2 Workstation
<LI>Gas Delivery System (GDS)
<LI>Pulmonary Function Module/Photoacoustic Analyzer Module (PFM/PAM)- provided by the European Space Agency (ESA)<END>
        </div>

